description:
Design a circuit that takes an 8-bit input from switches (sw) and translates it into an 8-bit output to LEDs (led) based on a clock signal. It utilizes a counter that increments on each positive clock edge, which effectively introduces a delay controlled by a specified parameter (LOG2DELAY). The final LED output reflects the upper 8 bits of the counter after shifting it right by LOG2DELAY bits, effectively creating a time-based representation of the counter’s state when monitored at the LED outputs.
module top_module(
    input  wire clk,

    input  wire [7:0] sw,
    output wire [7:0] led
);

