Design a 4-bit multiplier circuit that accepts two 4-bit inputs, A and B, and produces an 8-bit output, result. The implementation utilizes a combinational logic approach, iteratively checking each bit of input B; when a bit is high, it adds the corresponding left-shifted version of input A to a temporary accumulator. The final value of the accumulator represents the product of A and B, resulting in an 8-bit output that captures the full range of possible multiplication results within the specified input width.
