Design a circuit that extracts and extends immediate data from a 32-bit instruction input based on specific opcode bits. This functionality is achieved using a combinational logic block that interprets different instruction formats, with the output being a 64-bit immediate value. The immediate data is extended to ensure it aligns with the bit-width requirements of subsequent processing stages, enabling proper execution of operations dependent on immediate values in a CPU architecture.
