Design a circuit that generates a 6-bit counter (boxnum) which increments on every positive edge of the clock (clk). The counter resets to zero after reaching the value of 15. The current value of the counter is continuously outputted as boxnum. This implementation serves to create a simple sequential logic element that can be used for tasks such as tracking item counts or addressing in a finite domain.
module top_module(
input clk,
output reg [5:0]boxnum
    );

